{"reply":"In Chapter V, Squealer’s exact two sentences are: “Do not imagine, comrades, that leadership is a pleasure! On the contrary, it is a deep and heavy responsibility.”

The wording makes leadership sound like a burden Napoleon nobly accepts, while quietly presenting the animals’ own decision-making as a danger: they might make “the wrong decisions.” That framing turns the loss of a say into something supposedly protective. The change is concrete: decisions will be made privately by Napoleon’s committee, then communicated to the others; “there would be no more debates.”

That seems relevant to your project situation without proving that your lead’s motives are the same. Someone can genuinely feel responsible and still use that burden to close down questions. Your guilt may be worth separating from the question itself: asking why a plan changed is not the same as refusing to share responsibility. You can acknowledge the burden they describe while still wanting a say in decisions that affect your work.","evidence_uses":[{"source_kind":"book_corpus","evidence_id":"pga0100011-vc7ff4da7-ch05-ln1116-1143","source_location":"Chapter 5 — Chapter V, source lines 1116-1143","exact_quote":"Do not imagine, comrades, that leadership is a pleasure! On the contrary, it is a deep and heavy responsibility.","supported_claims":["Squealer’s exact two sentences are: “Do not imagine, comrades, that leadership is a pleasure! On the contrary, it is a deep and heavy responsibility.”","The wording makes leadership sound like a burden Napoleon nobly accepts, while quietly presenting the animals’ own decision-making as a danger: they might make “the wrong decisions.”","That framing turns the loss of a say into something supposedly protective."]},{"source_kind":"book_corpus","evidence_id":"pga0100011-vc7ff4da7-ch05-ln1096-1114","source_location":"Chapter 5 — Chapter V, source lines 1096-1114","exact_quote":"There would be no more debates.","supported_claims":["The change is concrete: decisions will be made privately by Napoleon’s committee, then communicated to the others; “there would be no more debates.”"]}],"memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}
